# Add or change a command

All of these, in one change (skip none):

1. Command module under `src/<proto>/commands/{downlink,uplink}/<name>.ts` (camelCase; file name === exported `name`)
2. Re-export in `commands/{downlink,uplink}/index.ts` (`export * as name from './name.js'`)
3. Id in `constants/{downlink,uplink}Ids.ts` (hardware-defined, not sequential). Names come from `invertObject` of ids
4. **Both** `toBytesMap[id]` and `fromBytesMap[id]` in `message/{down,up}link.ts`
5. At least one `examples` entry; `fromBytes` takes **body only** (no header)

Matching uplink/downlink ids must stay equal when both directions exist.

`tests/commands.consistency.test.ts` covers analog, analog-ultrasound, mtx1, mtx3, obis-observer, and plc.

MTX3: re-export the MTX1 module when the payload is identical; add a native file when it differs.

```ts
// BAD — fromBytesMap pointed at the encoder
fromBytesMap[cmd.id] = cmd.toBytes;

// GOOD
toBytesMap[cmd.id] = cmd.toBytes;
fromBytesMap[cmd.id] = cmd.fromBytes;
```
